➡️ℹ️🇩🇪 Lothar Matthäus felt an apology was the least Klopp could do after initially questioning Julian Nagelsmann's starting XI plans with Musiala;

"Klopp apologized to Nagelsmann after Sunday's game, saying, "Even at 59, I'm still an idiot ." That's typical Jürgen, cracking jokes like that because he sees he's made a mistake. He apologized, which was the least he could do. But something like that shouldn't have happened in the first place; it was very thoughtless."

[@SkySportDE]

